      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">Destination Handover, Odometer Sign-Off &amp; Joint Condition Inspection for Bike Transportation In Umarkote</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><p>When a Two‑Wheeler or Motorcycle arrives at its destination, the handover procedure is designed to guarantee that the vehicle’s condition, mileage, and documentation match the records captured at pickup. The process begins with a daylight visual inspection that compares the current state of the bike to the photographs taken at the point of dispatch.</p>
<p>This step is crucial for detecting any new scratches, dents, or fluid leaks that might have occurred during transit. The inspector notes any discrepancies on a standard condition checklist and photographs the bike again for the recipient’s reference.</p>

<p>Next, the odometer is read and recorded. The mileage shown on the motorcycle’s odometer must align with the figure listed on the Logistics Receipt (LR) bilty.</p>
<p>If the numbers match, the inspector writes “Mileage Verified” on the bilty and signs the verification stamp. In the event of a mismatch, the inspector documents the difference, informs the dispatch team, and the vehicle is temporarily held until the issue is resolved before final handover.</p>

<p>Once visual and mileage checks are complete, the handover moves to the signed condition sign‑off. Both the delivery agent and the recipient sign the condition report, confirming that the vehicle was received in the condition documented and that the odometer reading is accurate.</p>
<p>The signed report is then scanned into the company’s digital asset management system, and a hard copy is returned to the recipient as part of the final delivery documentation bundle.</p>

<p style="font-size: 1.04rem; line-height: 1.75; color: #f1f5f9; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 12px;">During the entire procedure, the inspector must follow the company’s safety protocol: wear a helmet, gloves, and ensure the bike is on a stable stand.</p>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 16px 0 20px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;"><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>All observations are logged in the mobile app, which automatically timestamps and geotags the handover location.</span></li><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>This digital trail ensures traceability, protects against disputes, and provides a clear audit trail for future reference.</span></li></ul>

